config AOC_USF_IIO
	tristate "AoC USF sensor framework to IIO bridge"
	depends on IIO
	depends on AOC_CHAN_DRIVER
	select AOC_USF_CORE
	select IIO_BUFFER
	select IIO_KFIFO_BUF
	help
	  Bridge the sensors hosted by the AoC USF (Unified Sensor Framework)
	  firmware on Google Tensor devices to Linux IIO. The AoC sensor
	  registry is loaded out of band by a userspace daemon; once it is
	  loaded, this driver enumerates the sensors over the com.google.usf
	  AOCC channel and exposes them as IIO devices (accelerometer,
	  gyroscope, magnetometer, light, proximity, pressure).

	  To compile this driver as a module, choose M here: the module will
	  be called aoc-usf-iio.

	  If unsure, say N.
